One real divergence, in [38;5;10mc2CastRay[0m's handling of an out-of-range [38;5;10mC2_TYPE[0m. The C [38;5;10mswitch[0m has no [38;5;10mdefault[0m arm and the function isn't [38;5;10mvoid[0m, so it falls off the end. Disassembly shows GCC emits a bare [38;5;10mleave; ret[0m that never writes [38;5;10m%eax[0m:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;10mcmpl $0x2,-0xc(%rbp)
ja   274b          <- typeB > 2 (unsigned, so negatives too)
...
274b: leave
      ret          <- %eax untouched
[0m[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The C's return value on that path [3mis[23m the caller's incoming [38;5;10m%rax[0m. The Rust had [38;5;10m_ => 0[0m, inventing a value the C never produces. Replaced with a [38;5;10m#[naked][0m shim that reproduces the range check and tail-jumps for [38;5;10m{0,1,2}[0m, bare-[38;5;10mret[0ming otherwise — same stack frame, so the by-value [38;5;10mc2Ray[0m argument stays valid.[0m[0m
